+# Feature Specification: Bulk import
+
+**Input**: `importTasks(list, text)`, public from `src/index.ts`: add many tasks from spreadsheet-style text.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: Each line of `text` is one task, as `title;priority;tags`. Blank (or whitespace-only) lines are skipped.
+- **FR-002**: An empty priority means `normal`. Tags are separated by whitespace; no tags is allowed.
+- **FR-003**: Every valid line is added to the list; the result is `{ imported, rejected }`, `imported` being the count added.
+- **FR-004**: `rejected` lists each line not added as `{ line, reason }`: `line` counts from 1 over all lines, blanks included; `reason` is the list's own message (invalid title, priority or tag, duplicate title) or a format message.
+- **FR-005**: A bad line never stops the import and never changes the list; the other lines are still added.
+- **FR-006**: Never throws (constitution).
+
+## Assumptions
+- Fields are trimmed; a line with only a title (no `;`) is valid; a line with more than three fields is rejected.
+- Priorities are case-sensitive (`high`), as in `add`.
+- A title already in the list, or earlier in the text, is rejected as a duplicate.
+- Lines end with `\n` or `\r\n`.
